│ Review background: Patient‐reported outcomes measures (PROMs) assess a patient’s subjective appraisal of health      │
│ outcomes from their own perspective. Despite hypothesised benefits that feedback on PROMs can support                │
│ decision‐making in clinical practice and improve outcomes, there is uncertainty surrounding the effectiveness of     │
│ PROMs feedback.                                                                                                      │
│ Review objective: To assess the effects of PROMs feedback to patients, or healthcare workers, or both on             │
