### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
Screening Criteria Applied:
- Population: Patients receiving healthcare services
- Intervention: PROMs feedback to healthcare professionals and/or patients
- Comparison: No feedback (usual care/control)
- Outcomes: Patient-reported health outcomes and processes of care
- Study Design: Randomized controlled trials

Screening Approach:
1. Conservative screening - when in doubt, include the study
2. Each study evaluated individually with specific rationale
3. Consideration of population, intervention, comparison, outcomes, and design
4. No keyword-only heuristics - careful reading of titles and abstracts

Review Protocol Context:
- Review Title: Routine provision of feedback from patient‐reported outcome measurements to healthcare providers and 
patients in clinical practice
- Review Objective: To assess the effects of PROMs feedback to patients, or healthcare workers, or both on 
patient‐reported health outcomes and processes of care.
- Selection Criteria: Two review authors independently screened and selected studies for inclusion. We included 
randomised trials directly comparing the effects on outcomes and processes of care of PROMs feedback to healthcare 
professionals and patients, or both with the impact of not providing such information.

All studies were screened against the requirement for randomized trials directly comparing PROMs feedback to healthcare 
professionals and/or patients with the impact of not providing such information, focusing on patient-reported health 
outcomes and processes of care.
